  "query_preview": "/Through Sunday/...\nIssued at 239 AM MDT Mon Jul 13 2026\n\nAn upper level high will continue from the central US into the \ncentral Rockies thru Thu.  There will still be just enough mid level \nmoisture, over the higher terrain, for isold to widely sct higher \nbased tstms this aftn.  Most of this activity will be along and \nsouth of I-70 in the mtns and over South Park.  Elsewhere it will \nremain dry and hot.\n\nFor Tue thru Thu, any monsoon moisture looks like it will stay over \nwrn CO into the Great Basin.  Thus any tstm activity over the higher \nterrain looks to be rather isold with dry conditions over the \nplains.  Temperatures will remain hot with 90's continuing over the \nplains.\n\nBy Fri thru next weekend, the center of the upper level high will be \nover the central Rockies.  Overall, it still appears the best fetch \nof monsoon moisture will generally stay to the west of the area with \nonly a slight chc of tstms over the higher terrain.  Temperatures \nwill remain above normal.\n\nEventually, the upper level high may shift a bit further south by \nthe following week which may allow for a better influx of monsoon \nmoisture and increasing tstm chances.",
